// Combat spell rows for magic_spell_table - the ONE pre-existing spell table declared in
// skill_magic/configs/magic.dbtable, which the utility spells (teleports, alchemy, enchant, charge
// orb) have always used. This file only adds rows to it; it declares no table of its own.
//
// History worth knowing (2026-09-04): these rows were first written against a brand-new parallel
// magic_spell_table/dbtable + a parallel set of ~10 support procs, on the belief that neither the
// table nor the procs existed. Both already did - get_spell_data/check_spell_requirements/
// delete_spell_runes/give_spell_xp/magic_spell_maxhit in skill_magic/scripts/magic.rs2,
// npc_projectile/player_projectile in skill_combat/scripts/projectile.rs2, player_autocast_enabled/
// player_autocast_reset in skill_combat/scripts/player/auto_cast.rs2, convert_stat_to_npc_stat in
// player/scripts/stat.rs2 - and the duplicates broke the build repo-wide. The duplicate table and
// support file are gone; these rows now use the real schema and the real procs. Full writeup in
// claude/ancient-magicks.md.
//
// Schema notes for this table (see magic.dbtable for the column list):
//  - runesrequired holds 3 fixed rune/count pairs, padded with null,null. The 8 Smoke/Shadow ancients
//    cost 4 different runes, so their non-elemental 4th rune goes in the rune4 column (added for
//    this); elemental runes always occupy the first 3 slots so staff substitution still works.
//  - spotanim_proj carries the spotanim PLUS the 7 projectile parameters (startheight, endheight,
//    delay, angle, length, offset, step) - the whole field expands into ~npc_projectile/
//    ~player_projectile's argument list at the call site. Every row here uses 43,31,51,16,-5,64,10,
//    this codebase's standard magic-projectile tuple (projectile.rs2's own "// wind" reference
//    example, and the firebolt/shooting-star call sites in nezikchened.rs2 and ghast.rs2 all use it).
//  - spotanim_target carries the spotanim plus its render height; 92 (body level) throughout, the
//    height this codebase uses for spell spotanims everywhere else.
//  - members is false on every row, preserving the original data's behaviour (it had no members flag
//    at all). Not strictly accurate - waves, binds, vulnerability/enfeeble/stun, magic dart and all
//    16 ancients were members-only in 2006 - but the column is now read by the real
//    check_spell_requirements, and false is the non-blocking choice. Worth setting accurately once
//    someone can test member-gating in-game.
//
// All level/rune/xp/maxhit figures below are the classic (2006-era, pre gear-scaling) OSRS values,
// cross-checked against the wiki. XP is stored *100 (fixed point), matching this repo's existing
// convention (see skill_cooking's cooking_generic.dbrow, e.g. stew = 1170 for 11.7 xp).
//
// Player cast anim/spotanim tags for the 26 normal spellbook rows are all directly confirmed against
// content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.seq and all.spotanim. sound_cast/sound_hit are left unpopulated
// everywhere: no all.synth or synth.pack exists anywhere in this repo, so there is no real tag to
// verify a sound name against for ANY spell (not just the new ones) - see the guard added in
// player_magic.rs2/npc_combat_magic.rs2 that makes sound_cast safely skippable instead of a hard error.

// ============================================================
// Normal spellbook - strike/bolt/blast/wave (16)
// ============================================================

[magic_combat_wind_strike]
table=magic_spell_table
data=spell,^wind_strike
data=members,false
data=name,"Wind Strike"
data=spellcom,magic:wind_strike
data=levelrequired,1
data=experience,550
data=maxhit,2
data=anim,human_caststrike
data=spotanim_origin,windstrike_casting
data=spotanim_proj,windstrike_travel,43,31,51,16,-5,64,10
data=spotanim_target,windstrike_impact,92
data=continue_by_autocast,yes
data=runesrequired,airrune,1,mindrune,1,null,null

